Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,RTLRefine: checked RTL repair with NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.\NInspect the failure, source diff and verification evidence in one browser.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.72,0:00:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring a Verilog/SystemVerilog ZIP and your own self-checking benches.\NSelect file roles in the browser, or include a manifest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.10,0:00:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,This authored integration example has two files and a 129-bit function.\NIts result should be a+b, but the implementation subtracts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.12,0:00:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,First reproduce the public failure using isolated native tools.\NChecking the original makes no model request.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.20,0:00:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The original fails its public test. No checked project is offered.\NThe tests remain immutable throughout the repair.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.28,0:00:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,A fresh NVIDIA request through Nebius Token Factory.\NThe model sees public checks; audit benches stay hidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.28,0:00:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Nemotron changes the subtraction to addition. The exact patch is rebuilt.\NBoth the public bench and the withheld 40-check audit pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.44,0:00:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Reimport the exported ZIP and run both benches again.\NThis fresh check makes no model request.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.95,0:00:58.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The exported project passes again. Its evidence includes logs and hashes.\NOriginal test files and the project license are preserved.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.57,0:01:06.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Now upload an intentionally incomplete developer-written patch.\NChanging the project removes the previous successful verdict immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.58,0:01:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The partial patch passes the public bench and fails the audit.\NA checked download is blocked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.03,0:01:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Rejected with the failing observations retained.\NAcceptance covers only the supplied tests, not unbounded hardware correctness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.43,0:01:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Historical examples: the same 118 candidates take 208.08s vs 13.87s.\N15.0x screening throughput; matching results, one paired run per profile.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.44,0:01:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,This screening measurement does not apply to uploaded projects.\NTheir exact files are compiled independently using the supplied benches.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.04,0:01:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Public source and a Docker test build: github.com/ehdtjq08/RTLRefine\NRecorded NVIDIA runs and fresh native checks work without an API key.
